# SPROTO FISHING — Web3 fishing game on Robinhood Chain (EVM, chainId 4663)
#
# Copy to .env.local for local dev. Set the same vars in the Vercel project
# settings for production. VITE_-prefixed vars are inlined into the client
# bundle at BUILD time — changing one requires a redeploy, not just a restart.

# --- Client (VITE_, safe to expose) ---------------------------------------

# Robinhood Chain RPC. Defaults to the public endpoint.
# VITE_ROBINHOOD_RPC_URL=https://rpc.mainnet.chain.robinhood.com

# The $BITCOIN game token — HarryPotterObamaSonic10Inu, 8 decimals. Drives
# the wallet balance panel, the title-screen market-cap pill, the contract-
# address footer, and the burn-to-unlock buttons for gear and locations.
#
# WARNING: 0x72e4f9F8... is deployed on ETHEREUM MAINNET (chainId 1). The
# game transacts on Robinhood Chain (4663), where that address has no code
# (verified: eth_getCode returns 0 bytes). Until the token exists on 4663,
# on-chain reads, burns and withdrawals will fail.
# VITE_GAME_TOKEN_ADDRESS=0x72e4f9F808C49A2a61dE9C5896298920Dc4EEEa9
# VITE_GAME_TOKEN_SYMBOL=$BITCOIN
# VITE_GAME_TOKEN_DECIMALS=8
# VITE_GAME_TOKEN_CHAIN_ID=1

# Treasury that receives in-game purchases.
# VITE_GAME_TREASURY=

# Backend API base. Leave unset to route through the Vercel /api/backend
# proxy (which forwards to RENDER_API_BASE below).
# VITE_API_URL=

# --- Server-only (no VITE_ prefix — never reaches the client bundle) -------

# The Render API service for SPROTO FISHING. Required: /api/backend returns
# 503 until this is set. Render appends a random suffix, so copy the exact
# URL from the Render dashboard.
# RENDER_API_BASE=https://sproto-fishing-XXXX.onrender.com

# Treasury private key that signs every /api/withdraw transaction. Without
# it, /api/withdraw returns 503 "Withdrawals not configured".
# Set this directly in the Vercel dashboard — never commit it.
# SPROTO_TREASURY_SECRET=

# Max $BITCOIN allowed per single /api/withdraw call. Defaults to 100,000,000.
# SPROTO_WITHDRAW_MAX=100000000
